  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nStep 8 of the [transfer steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#the-offscreencanvas-interface:transfer-steps) tells you to encode a weak reference to a Canvas in a different realm. But in [the definition for transfer steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/structured-data.html#transfer-steps) it requires \"The resulting data held in dataHolder must be independent of any [realm](https://tc39.es/ecma262/#sec-code-realms).\" I don't see how holding a reference to an object in another realm could be realm independent.",
